# Production verification after deployment

Use a normal purchaser account, not an admin account:

1. Open `/workshops/before-start~ubuuc/office-hours~3cmbs`.
2. Confirm the lesson stays on the lesson route and renders six `Watch Replay` links.
3. Confirm the browser makes no `/api/resources?...type=cohort` request.
4. Open each replay link and confirm HTTP 200.
5. In an anonymous browser, open the same lesson route.
6. Confirm it redirects to `/workshops/before-start~ubuuc` and no office-hours title, recording link, or session payload appears.
7. Confirm the unauthenticated generic resource request remains HTTP 401.

# Residual risks

- Post-deploy purchaser readback is still required because this worker neither deployed nor mutated production.
- The server returns nothing if the request cannot read the protected workshop or the authored cohort lacks an active relation to it. Expected access and relation misses are not error-logged.
- The query is intentionally uncached. Authorized renders repeat the request-bound workshop check, then add one narrow, schema-checked database read.
